---
title: Synapse — how the pieces fit
---
%% Colour carries the lane: what the MODEL judges, what a SCRIPT executes, what
%% lands in the VAULT. Subgraphs carry the phase. The seam is visible as the only
%% two arrows that leave a yellow box for a blue one -- manifest.tsv and b-NN.md.
flowchart TB
    classDef model fill:#ffec99,stroke:#e8590c,color:#1e1e1e
    classDef seam fill:#ffc9c9,stroke:#c2255c,color:#1e1e1e,stroke-width:3px
    classDef script fill:#d0ebff,stroke:#1971c2,color:#1e1e1e
    classDef vault fill:#d3f9d8,stroke:#2f9e44,color:#1e1e1e
    classDef hook fill:#ffd8a8,stroke:#e8590c,color:#1e1e1e
    classDef cmd fill:#e5dbff,stroke:#6741d9,color:#1e1e1e

    subgraph BUILD["BUILD · /synapse-init"]
        direction TB
        ORIENT["<b>model</b><br/>orientation pass<br/>read the repo, aggregate paths,<br/>cluster into nodes"]
        MANIFEST["<b>manifest.tsv — THE SEAM</b><br/>title ⇥ include-ERE ⇥ exclude-ERE<br/>one line per node"]
        LISTS["synapse-build-lists.sh<br/>git ls-files → all.txt<br/>expand the manifest → lists/NN.txt<br/>prints enumerated / covered / unassigned"]
        PROSE["<b>model</b><br/>author prose per node → b-NN.md<br/>summary · crux <i>pointer</i> · links<br/>+ grounded_in pointers"]
        PUSH["synapse-push-nodes.sh<br/>loops every node with both<br/>a path list and a body"]
        WRITE["synapse-write-node.sh<br/>hash every path · sources_digest<br/>slice the crux from its pointer<br/>digest each grounded_in range<br/>aggregate ## Sources · record commit"]
        IDX["synapse-build-index.sh"]
        PIDX["synapse-build-project-index.sh"]
        TAGS["synapse-tags.sh<br/>tree-sitter defs + refs<br/>optional, falls back to reading"]

        TAGS -.->|"clustering signal"| ORIENT
        ORIENT -->|"authors"| MANIFEST
        MANIFEST --> LISTS
        MANIFEST --> PROSE
        LISTS -->|"lists/NN.txt"| PUSH
        PROSE -->|"b-NN.md"| PUSH
        PUSH -->|"per node"| WRITE
        WRITE --> IDX --> PIDX
    end

    subgraph VAULT["VAULT · synapse/{repo}@{branch}/"]
        direction LR
        NODE["{Node Title}.md × N<br/>sources · sources_digest · commit<br/>crux_path · grounded_in · stale<br/>fenced prose + human ## Notes"]
        JSON["_index.json<br/>source path → owning nodes"]
        INDEX["Index.md<br/>node map + remote + branch"]
        AUX["_manifest.tsv · _profile.txt<br/>kept for the next rebuild"]
        TAGSCACHE["_tags_cache.json<br/>path → {hash, tags, unsupported}<br/>machine-only, never authoritative"]
    end

    WRITE ==>|"PUT over the local REST API"| NODE
    IDX ==> JSON
    PIDX ==> INDEX
    WRITE -.->|"byproduct: refreshes<br/>via synapse-tags-cache.sh<br/>(best-effort, non-fatal)"| TAGSCACHE

    subgraph USE["READ · DETECT · REPAIR"]
        direction TB
        QUERY["synapse-query.sh<br/>body · sources · field<br/>reads the expensive parts internally,<br/>prints only the projection asked for"]
        SYMBOL["synapse-query.sh symbol<br/>exact-name def/ref lookup —<br/>cache read, lazy xargs -P backfill<br/>on a miss (synapse-tags-cache.sh)"]
        NODESKILL["synapse-node skill<br/>Tier 2: verify, then regenerate lazily"]
        STALE1["synapse-staleness.sh<br/>Tier 1 hook: stale: true,<br/>+ correction nudge when cited<br/>evidence stops matching"]
        STALE2["synapse-query.sh stale<br/>re-hashes what a node claims —<br/>but a rename reads as gone"]
        DRIFT["synapse-query.sh drift<br/>diffs commit..HEAD: the only thing<br/>that sees ADDED paths, deletes,<br/>renames and baseline divergence"]
        GROUND["synapse-query.sh grounding<br/>re-slices cited evidence:<br/>moved → re-point, changed → re-check"]
        REBUILD["/synapse-rebuild<br/>triage per node:<br/>reseat · patch from diff · re-orient"]
        CLEAN["synapse-graph-clean.sh<br/>removes a namespace whose upstream<br/>is gone; reports what it cannot<br/>confirm. Run, never fired."]

        DRIFT --> REBUILD
        GROUND --> REBUILD
    end

    NODE -.->|"read"| QUERY
    NODE -.-> NODESKILL
    JSON -.-> STALE1
    NODE -.-> STALE2
    NODE -.-> DRIFT
    NODE -.-> GROUND
    NODE -.->|"sources"| SYMBOL
    TAGSCACHE -.->|"read"| SYMBOL
    SYMBOL -.->|"backfill on miss"| TAGSCACHE
    REBUILD ==>|"re-writes each node,<br/>re-recording its commit"| WRITE
    CLEAN -.->|"deletes the whole<br/>namespace when its<br/>branch is gone"| NODE

    class ORIENT,PROSE model
    class MANIFEST seam
    class LISTS,PUSH,WRITE,IDX,PIDX,TAGS,QUERY,SYMBOL,STALE2,DRIFT,GROUND,CLEAN script
    class NODE,JSON,INDEX,AUX,TAGSCACHE vault
    class STALE1 hook
    class REBUILD,NODESKILL cmd

    subgraph KEY["the colours"]
        direction LR
        K1["model judgment"]
        K2["the seam"]
        K3["script — mechanics"]
        K4["vault artifact"]
        K5["fires automatically"]
        K6["command / skill"]
    end
    class K1 model
    class K2 seam
    class K3 script
    class K4 vault
    class K5 hook
    class K6 cmd

    %% Neutral subgraph fills: the default pale yellow competes with the model
    %% lane's own yellow, and the point of the palette is that the lane is
    %% readable at a glance.
    style BUILD fill:#ffffff,stroke:#adb5bd,stroke-dasharray:4 4
    style VAULT fill:#ffffff,stroke:#adb5bd,stroke-dasharray:4 4
    style USE fill:#ffffff,stroke:#adb5bd,stroke-dasharray:4 4
    style KEY fill:#ffffff,stroke:#adb5bd,stroke-dasharray:4 4
